  "notes": [
    "Only 'Batas Definitif' rests on a signed regulation. 'Hasil Kesepakatan' is agreed by the villages and checked by BIG; 'Batas Indikatif' is a working line. UU 4/2011 Pasal 16 ayat (2): show boundaries that are not definitive with a different line style or colour, and never present any of them as a legal boundary.",
    "Use for maps, filters and 'which village is this point in' hints; let users correct the village they chose. Credit: Sumber: Badan Informasi Geospasial.",
    "District areas equal BIG's own district layer (BATAS_KECAMATAN_AR) to four decimals, except in districts with undefined areas (TIPADM 999: islands or water without a village, `undefined_areas` per regency), which BIG's district polygon includes and no village does.",
    "Borders between regencies are cut at the same points and simplified the same way on both sides (`shared_regency_border_arcs`); arcs that would make a ring collapse or cross itself or another ring are kept finer (`arcs_with_smaller_tolerance`), so no two villages overlap. `largest_area_change_percent` compares the simplified with the full-precision area; small villages change most."
  ]
}
